kind":"message","text":"To find the sum of the decimal digits of $2^{50}$, we first compute the exact value of $2^{50}$:\n\nUsing known powers of 2:\n$$2^{10} = 1,024$$\n$$2^{20} = 1,048,576$$\n$$2^{30} = 1,073,741,824$$\n$$2^{40} = 1,099,511,627,776$$\n\nMultiplying $2^{40}$ by $2^{10} = 1,024$:\n$$2^{50} = 1,099,511,627,776 \\times 1,024 = 1,125,899,906,842,624$$\n\nNow, we sum the digits of $1,125,899,906,842,624$:\n$$1 + 1 + 2 + 5 + 8 + 9 + 9 + 9 + 0 + 6 + 8 + 4 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 76$$\n\nWe can also verify using modulo 9:\n$$2^{50} \\equiv (2^6)^8 \\times 2^2 \\equiv 1^8 \\times 4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 9$$\n$$76 \\equiv 7 + 6 = 13 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 9$$\n\nFinal: 76","t":18.2},{"type":"status","node":"b","status":"done","t":18.2},{"type":"usage","node":"c","tokens_in":79,"tokens_out":271,"usd":0.0008525,"estimated":false,"model":"sonnet","t":19.1},{"type":"message","from":"c","to":"exchange_fn","edge":"e6","port":"c","kind":"message","text":"To find the sum of the decimal digits of $2^{50}$, we first calculate the exact value of $2^{50}$:\n\n$$2^{10} = 1024$$\n$$2^{20} = 1024^2 = 1,048,576$$\n$$2^{40} = (1,048,576)^2 = 1,099,511,627,776$$\n$$2^{50} = 2^{40} \\times 2^{10} = 1,099,511,627,776 \\times 1024 = 1,125,899,906,842,624$$\n\nNow, we sum the digits of $1,125,899,906,842,624$:\n$$1 + 1 + 2 + 5 + 8 + 9 + 9 + 9 + 0 + 6 + 8 + 4 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 76$$\n\nFinal: 76","t":19.1},{"type":"status","node":"c","status":"done","t":19.1},{"type":"status","node":"exchange_fn","status":"working","t":19.1},{"type":"transform","at":"exchange_fn","label":"js function","detail":"→ out: Paradigm: memory. All three agree after round 1.\nFinal: 76","t":19.1},{"type":"message","from":"exchange_fn","to":"exchange","edge":"e9","port":"answer","kind":"message","text":"Paradigm: memory. All three agree after round 1.\nFinal: 76","t":19.1},{"type":"transform","at":"exchange","label":"rounds done","detail":"output.done holds (round 1)","t":19.1},{"type":"message","from":"exchange","to":"user"